            </div>
            <div class="card-body" style="padding: 0;">
                <p>The formula for linear thermal expansion is:</p>
                <div class="formula-display" style="padding: 1rem; font-size: 1.2rem;">
                    $$ \Delta L = \alpha L_0 \Delta T $$
                </div>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>$\Delta L$</strong>: The change in length (how much it grew or shrank).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>$\alpha$ (Alpha)</strong>: The coefficient of linear expansion (a material constant).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>$L_0$</strong>: The original length of the object before temperature change.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>$\Delta T$</strong>: The change in temperature ($T_{final} - T_{initial}$).</li>
