                <div class="card-header">
                    <span><i class="icon">📝</i> Summary</span>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>In a spring-mass system, the stiffness constant ($k$) is inversely proportional to the square root of the period ($T$). Increasing the stiffness makes the restoring force stronger, causing the mass to accelerate more rapidly towards equilibrium, thereby increasing the frequency of oscillation.</p>
