          The <strong style={{ color: C.textPrimary }}>circular orbital speed</strong> is the precise tangential velocity at which gravitational attraction exactly supplies the centripetal force for a circular path. Reducing velocity below this threshold means gravity <em>overcomes</em> the centripetal balance — the planet begins to fall inward, converting the circular orbit into an <strong style={{ color: C.accentText }}>ellipse</strong> with the point of reduction becoming the <strong style={{ color: C.teal }}>apoapsis</strong>.
        </p>
      </Card>

      {/* ── Circular Speed Formula ── */}
      <FormulaCard
        title="Circular Orbital Speed"
        tex="v_c = \sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}"
        explanation={[
          "G is the gravitational constant (6.674 × 10⁻¹¹ N m² kg⁻²).",
          "M is the mass of the central body (star or planet being orbited).",
          "r is the orbital radius — distance from the centre of the central body.",
          "This formula is derived by equating gravitational force to centripetal force: GMm/r² = mv²/r.",
          "Any velocity below this value means gravity dominates — the orbit shrinks inward.",
        ]}
        lab={{
          title: "Circular Speed",
          description: "Compute circular orbital speed for different star masses and orbital radii.",
          formula: {
            compute: ({ M, r }) => ({
              value: Math.sqrt(6.674e-11 * M * 1e30 / (r * 1e11)),
              unit: "m/s",
              decimals: 0,
            }),
          },
          variables: [
            { key: "M", label: "M", name: "Star mass", default: 1.0, min: 0.1, max: 5, step: 0.1, unit: "M☉", decimals: 1 },
            { key: "r", label: "r", name: "Orbital radius", default: 1.0, min: 0.1, max: 5, step: 0.1, unit: "AU", decimals: 1 },
          ],
        }}
      />

      {/* ── Step-by-Step ── */}
      <KeplerCard />

      {/* ── Live Explorer ── */}
      <LiveOrbitExplorer />

      {/* ── Vis Viva Formula ── */}
      <FormulaCard
        title="Vis-Viva Equation"
        tex="v^2 = GM\left(\frac{2}{r} - \frac{1}{a}\right)"
        accentColor={C.teal}
        explanation={[
          "This is the master equation linking speed, position, and orbit shape.",
          "a is the semi-major axis of the ellipse. For a circle, a = r and v = v_c.",
          "When v < v_c at radius r, the semi-major axis a shrinks below r — confirming the orbit tightens.",
          "At periapsis, r is minimum and v is maximum. At apoapsis, r is maximum and v is minimum.",
          "The equation is a direct consequence of conservation of mechanical energy.",
        ]}
        lab={{
          title: "Vis-Viva",
          description: "Find orbital speed at any point on the ellipse given semi-major axis and current radius.",
          formula: {
            compute: ({ r, a, M }) => {
              const v2 = 6.674e-11 * M * 1e30 * (2 / (r * 1e11) - 1 / (a * 1e11));
              return { value: v2 > 0 ? Math.sqrt(v2) : 0, unit: "m/s", decimals: 0 };
            },
          },
          variables: [
            { key: "M", label: "M", name: "Star mass", default: 1.0, min: 0.1, max: 5, step: 0.1, unit: "M☉", decimals: 1 },
            { key: "r", label: "r", name: "Current radius", default: 1.0, min: 0.1, max: 4, step: 0.05, unit: "AU", decimals: 2 },
            { key: "a", label: "a", name: "Semi-major axis", default: 0.8, min: 0.1, max: 4, step: 0.05, unit: "AU", decimals: 2 },
          ],
        }}
      />

      {/* ── Energy ── */}
      <EnergyCard />

      {/* ── Comparison Table ── */}
      <ComparisonTable />

      {/* ── Key Consequences ── */}
      <Card>
        <SectionLabel icon="💡" text="Key Physical Consequences" color={C.amber} />
        {[
          {
            icon: "🔁",
            title: "Orbit Becomes Elliptical",
            body: "The point where velocity was reduced becomes the apoapsis. The planet falls to a lower periapsis on the opposite side.",
            color: C.accent,
          },
          {
            icon: "⚡",
            title: "Speed Increases at Periapsis",
            body: "By conservation of angular momentum (L = mvr = const), the planet must speed up as it moves closer to the star.",
            color: C.teal,
          },
          {
            icon: "📉",
            title: "Total Energy Decreases",
            body: "The orbit has lower total mechanical energy than the original circular orbit. More negative E means a tighter, smaller ellipse.",
            color: C.green,
          },
          {
            icon: "⏱",
            title: "Orbital Period Changes",
            body: "By Kepler's Third Law, T² ∝ a³. A smaller semi-major axis means a shorter orbital period.",
            color: C.amber,
          },
        ].map((item, i) => (
          <div
            key={i}
            style={{
              display: "flex",
              gap: 14,
              padding: "12px 0",
              borderBottom: i < 3 ? `1px solid ${C.divider}` : "none",
            }}
          >
            <div
              style={{
                width: 36,
                height: 36,
                borderRadius: 10,
                background: item.color + "22",
                display: "flex",
                alignItems: "center",
                justifyContent: "center",
                fontSize: 18,
                flexShrink: 0,
              }}
            >
              {item.icon}
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style={{ fontSize: 13, fontWeight: 700, color: item.color, marginBottom: 4 }}>
                {item.title}
              </div>
              <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: C.textSecondary, lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                {item.body}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </Card>

      {/* ── Kepler T3 Formula ── */}
      <FormulaCard
        title="Kepler's Third Law"
        tex="T^2 = \frac{4\pi^2}{GM}\, a^3"
        accentColor={C.amber}
        explanation={[
          "T is the orbital period — time for one complete orbit.",
          "a is the semi-major axis of the ellipse.",
          "When v drops below v_c, the new ellipse has a smaller semi-major axis.",
          "Smaller a → smaller T. The planet completes orbits faster than it did on the original circle.",
          "This is how mission designers plan Hohmann transfer burns — reducing speed lowers the orbit.",
        ]}
      />

      {/* ── Summary ── */}
      <Card accent={C.accent} style={{ background: "#13162a" }}>
        <SectionLabel icon="📋" text="Summary" color={C.accentText} />
        <div style={{ display: "flex", flexDirection: "column", gap: 10 }}>
          {[
            ["Velocity reduced below v_c", "Gravity exceeds centripetal need → net inward force"],
            ["Orbit shape", "Circular → Elliptical (reduction point = apoapsis)"],
            ["Energy", "Total E decreases; orbit is more tightly bound"],
            ["Speed variation", "Faster at periapsis, slower at apoapsis (angular momentum conservation)"],
            ["Period", "Shorter — smaller semi-major axis by Kepler's Third Law"],
          ].map(([k, v], i) => (
            <div key={i} style={{ display: "flex", gap: 12, alignItems: "flex-start" }}>
              <span style={{ color: C.accent, fontSize: 13, marginTop: 2 }}>▸</span>
              <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: C.textSecondary, lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                <strong style={{ color: C.textPrimary }}>{k}:</strong> {v}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </Card>
    </div>
  );
}
