The core answer to your question: when **μ → 0**, deceleration = 0, stopping distance = ∞, and the block obeys **Newton's First Law** — sliding at constant velocity forever.

I'll build this as a proper interactive textbook experience with structured UI cards, formula cards, and a live physics sandbox.

```tsx
import { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from "react";
import { motion, AnimatePresence } from "framer-motion";

// ============================================================
// TYPES
// ============================================================
interface FormulaData {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  latex: string;
  variables: { symbol: string; description: string; range?: string }[];
  context: string;
}

