<body>

    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>Collision of Equal Masses</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Interactive Physics Module • 1D Kinematics</div>
        </header>

        <!-- Card 1: Introduction -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <span>Introduction</span>
                <span class="tag tag-blue">Concept</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <p>
                    When two objects of <strong>equal mass</strong> collide in one dimension, the outcome depends heavily on the elasticity of the collision. This scenario is a classic physics problem that simplifies the laws of conservation of momentum and energy.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Consider two carts or balls on a frictionless track. If Cart A approaches stationary Cart B, what happens after they hit? Do they bounce? Do they stick?
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 2: Key Concepts -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <span>Key Concepts</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <p>To understand the outcome, we must define two fundamental conservation laws that govern the system:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;"><strong>Conservation of Momentum:</strong> The total momentum of the system remains constant before and after the collision, provided no external forces act on it.</li>
                    <li style="margin-left: 20px;"><strong>Conservation of Kinetic Energy:</strong> In a perfectly elastic collision, the total kinetic energy is conserved. In inelastic collisions, some energy is transformed into heat or deformation.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 3: Formula Card (Momentum) -->
        <article class="card formula-card" id="formula-momentum">
            <div class="card-header">
                <span>Conservation Law</span>
                <span class="tag tag-green">Core Formula</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <p>For any collision (elastic or inelastic) between two masses $m_1$ and $m_2$:</p>

                <div class="formula-display">
                    $$m_1 v_{1i} + m_2 v_{2i} = m_1 v_{1f} + m_2 v_{2f}$$
                </div>

                <p>Since the masses are equal ($m_1 = m_2 = m$), the mass terms cancel out, simplifying the relationship between velocities:</p>

                <div class="formula-display">
                    $$v_{1i} + v_{2i} = v_{1f} + v_{2f}$$
                </div>

                <div class="formula-actions">
                    <button class="btn btn-outline" onclick="openExplanation('momentum')">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253"></path></svg>
                        Explain Formula
                    </button>
                    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="openLab()">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.752 11.168l-3.197-2.132A1 1 0 0010 9.87v4.263a1 1 0 001.555.832l3.197-2.132a1 1 0 000-1.664z"></path><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
                        Open Formula Lab
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 4: Comparison Table -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <span>Collision Outcomes</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <p>The behavior of the two masses differs drastically based on elasticity. Assume Mass A moves at velocity $v$ and Mass B is at rest ($0$).</p>
                <div class="table-responsive" style="margin-top: 16px;">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Type</th>
                                <th>Post-Collision Velocities</th>
                                <th>Energy</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Perfectly Elastic</strong></td>
                                <td>Mass A stops ($0$).<br>Mass B moves at $v$.</td>
                                <td>Conserved</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Perfectly Inelastic</strong></td>
                                <td>Both stick together.<br>Move at $v/2$.</td>
                                <td>Lost (Max loss)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 5: Summary -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <span>Summary</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-content">
                <p>
                    In collisions between equal masses, momentum conservation dictates that the vector sum of velocities remains constant. In the special case of a head-on elastic collision, the objects effectively "exchange" velocities.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If a moving object hits a stationary object of the same mass elastically, the moving object stops dead, and the stationary object flies away with the original speed.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>

    </div>

    <!-- Modal: Explanation -->
    <div class="modal-overlay" id="explanation-modal">
        <div class="modal">
            <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeModals()">&times;</button>
            <h2 class="modal-title">Formula Explanation</h2>
            <div class="explanation-content" id="explanation-text">
                <!-- Content injected via JS -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Modal: Formula Lab (Sandbox) -->
    <div class="modal-overlay" id="lab-modal">
        <div class="modal" style="max-width: 700px;">
            <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeModals()">&times;</button>
            <h2 class="modal-title">Collision Sandbox</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 16px;">
                Adjust the Coefficient of Restitution to switch between Elastic and Inelastic collisions.
            </p>

            <div class="lab-canvas-container">
                <canvas id="simCanvas"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="controls">
                <div class="control-group">
                    <label>Restitution (Bounciness): <span id="restitution-val" class="value-display">1.0</span></label>
                    <input type="range" id="restitution-slider" min="0" max="1" step="0.1" value="1">
                    <small style="color: #6b7280;">1.0 = Elastic, 0.0 = Inelastic</small>
                </div>
                <div class="control-group" style="justify-content: flex-end;">
                    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="resetSimulation()">Restart Collision</button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding: 12px; background: #f0fdf4; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #166534;">
                <strong>Observation:</strong> <span id="lab-observation">Set restitution to 1.0 and observe the velocity exchange.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- KaTeX JS -->
    <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.8/dist/katex.min.js"></script>
    <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.8/dist/contrib/auto-render.min.js" onload="renderMathInElement(document.body);"></script>

    <script>
        // --- Data for Formula Explanation ---
        const formulaData = {
            momentum: {
                title: "Conservation of Momentum",
                text: `
                    <p>This formula states that the total momentum of an isolated system remains constant. In the context of equal masses colliding:</p>
                    <p>Before collision, the total momentum is the sum of individual momentums ($mv$). After collision, it is the sum of the final momentums.</p>
                    <p>Because mass $m$ is the same for both objects, we can divide the entire equation by $m$, leaving us with a simple relationship between velocities:</p>
                    <div style="text-align:center; padding: 10px;">$$v_{1i} + v_{2i} = v_{1f} + v_{2f}$$</div>
                    <p>This means the <em>sum</em> of the velocities must be the same before and after impact.</p>
                    <ul class="variable-list">
                        <li><span class="variable-symbol">m</span> Mass of the object (kg)</li>
                        <li><span class="variable-symbol">v</span> Velocity (m/s)</li>
                        <li><span class="variable-symbol">i</span> Initial state (before collision)</li>
                        <li><span class="variable-symbol">f</span> Final state (after collision)</li>
                    </ul>
                `
            }
        };

        // --- Modal Handling ---
        function openExplanation(type) {
            const modal = document.getElementById('explanation-modal');
            const content = document.getElementById('explanation-text');

            if (formulaData[type]) {
                content.innerHTML = formulaData[type].text;
                // Re-render math in the modal
                renderMathInElement(content);
            }

            modal.classList.add('active');
        }

        function openLab() {
            const modal = document.getElementById('lab-modal');
            modal.classList.add('active');
            resetSimulation();
            animate();
        }

        function closeModals() {
            document.querySelectorAll('.modal-overlay').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('active'));
            stopAnimation();
        }

        // Close modal on click outside
        window.onclick = function(event) {
            if (event.target.classList.contains('modal-overlay')) {
                closeModals();
            }
        }

        // --- Collision Simulation Logic (Canvas) ---
        const canvas = document.getElementById('simCanvas');
        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
        let animationId;
        let isRunning = false;

        // Simulation State
        let balls = [];
        const restitutionSlider = document.getElementById('restitution-slider');
        const restitutionVal = document.getElementById('restitution-val');
        const observationText = document.getElementById('lab-observation');

        // Setup Canvas Resolution
        function resizeCanvas() {
            canvas.width = canvas.parentElement.clientWidth;
            canvas.height = 200;
        }
        window.addEventListener('resize', resizeCanvas);
        resizeCanvas();

        class Ball {
            constructor(x, radius, color, label) {
                this.x = x;
                this.y = canvas.height / 2;
                this.radius = radius;
                this.color = color;
                this.label = label;
                this.vx = 0;
                this.mass = 1; // Equal mass
            }

            draw() {
                // Draw Ball
                ctx.beginPath();
                ctx.arc(this.x, this.y, this.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
                ctx.fillStyle = this.color;
                ctx.fill();
                ctx.strokeStyle = '#333';
                ctx.lineWidth = 2;
                ctx.stroke();
                ctx.closePath();

                // Draw Label
                ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';
                ctx.font = 'bold 16px Inter';
                ctx.textAlign = 'center';
                ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
                ctx.fillText(this.label, this.x, this.y);

                // Draw Velocity Vector
                if (Math.abs(this.vx) > 0.1) {
                    ctx.beginPath();
                    ctx.moveTo(this.x, this.y - this.radius - 10);
                    ctx.lineTo(this.x + this.vx * 20, this.y - this.radius - 10); // Scale vector for visibility
                    ctx.strokeStyle = '#2563eb';
                    ctx.lineWidth = 3;
                    ctx.stroke();

                    // Arrowhead
                    ctx.beginPath();
                    const dir = this.vx > 0 ? 1 : -1;
                    ctx.moveTo(this.x + this.vx * 20, this.y - this.radius - 10);
                    ctx.lineTo(this.x + this.vx * 20 - (5 * dir), this.y - this.radius - 15);
                    ctx.lineTo(this.x + this.vx * 20 - (5 * dir), this.y - this.radius - 5);
                    ctx.lineTo(this.x + this.vx * 20, this.y - this.radius - 10);
                    ctx.fillStyle = '#2563eb';
                    ctx.fill();
                }
            }

            update() {
                this.x += this.vx;

                // Wall Collisions
                if (this.x - this.radius < 0) {
                    this.x = this.radius;
                    this.vx *= -1;
                }
                if (this.x + this.radius > canvas.width) {
                    this.x = canvas.width - this.radius;
                    this.vx *= -1;
                }
            }
        }

        function resetSimulation() {
            balls = [
                new Ball(100, 25, '#ef4444', 'A'), // Red
                new Ball(400, 25, '#3b82f6', 'B')  // Blue
            ];

            // Initial Conditions: A moves right at 4, B is stationary
            balls[0].vx = 4; 
            balls[1].vx = 0;

            updateObservation();
        }

        function updateObservation() {
            const e = parseFloat(restitutionSlider.value);
            if (e === 1) {
                observationText.innerText = "Elastic: Mass A stops, Mass B takes off at A's speed.";
            } else if (e === 0) {
                observationText.innerText = "Inelastic: Both masses stick together and move at half speed.";
            } else {
                observationText.innerText = `Partially Elastic (e=${e}): Masses separate but lose some speed.`;
            }
        }

        restitutionSlider.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
            restitutionVal.innerText = parseFloat(e.target.value).toFixed(1);
            updateObservation();
            // Optional: Reset sim when slider changes to avoid chaos
            resetSimulation();
        });

        function checkCollision(b1, b2) {
            const dx = b2.x - b1.x;
            const dist = Math.abs(dx);
            const minDist = b1.radius + b2.radius;

            if (dist < minDist) {
                // Resolve overlap to prevent sticking
                const overlap = minDist - dist;
                b1.x -= overlap / 2;
                b2.x += overlap / 2;

                // 1D Collision Formula with Coefficient of Restitution (e)
                // v1_final = ( (m1 - e*m2)*v1 + (1+e)*m2*v2 ) / (m1+m2)
                // Since m1 = m2 = 1:
                // v1_final = ( (1 - e)*v1 + (1+e)*v2 ) / 2
                // v2_final = ( (1+e)*v1 + (1 - e)*v2 ) / 2

                const e = parseFloat(restitutionSlider.value);
                const v1 = b1.vx;
                const v2 = b2.vx;

                b1.vx = ((1 - e) * v1 + (1 + e) * v2) / 2;
                b2.vx = ((1 + e) * v1 + (1 - e) * v2) / 2;
            }
        }

        function animate() {
            if (!isRunning) return;

            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

            // Draw Floor Line
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(0, canvas.height/2 + 25);
            ctx.lineTo(canvas.width, canvas.height/2 + 25);
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#e5e7eb';
            ctx.lineWidth = 2;
            ctx.stroke();

            balls.forEach(ball => {
                ball.update();
                ball.draw();
            });

            checkCollision(balls[0], balls[1]);

            animationId = requestAnimationFrame(animate);
        }

        function startAnimation() {
            if (!isRunning) {
                isRunning = true;
                animate();
            }
        }

        function stopAnimation() {
            isRunning = false;
            cancelAnimationFrame(animationId);
        }

        // Initialize simulation but don't start loop until modal opens
        resizeCanvas();
        resetSimulation();

        // Override reset button to ensure animation starts
        const originalReset = resetSimulation;
        resetSimulation = function() {
            originalReset();
            startAnimation();
        };

    </script>
</body>
</html>
